James sought an alternative term for "plausible worst-case scenario" that conveys a high-risk possibility without using the word "risk." I suggested several options, emphasizing clarity and appropriateness for various contexts. The recommended terms included **“severe plausible scenario”** for general audiences, as well as **“adverse scenario,” “high-impact scenario,”** and **“stress scenario”** for more specific applications. Additionally, I offered **“pessimistic scenario,” “challenging scenario,”** and **“upper-plausible scenario”** as softer or more technical alternatives. The focus was on providing terms that effectively communicate the concept with less alarmist connotations.
